// v3.std.coproduct_projection — Variant-aware projection metadata
// carrier for coproduct response bodies.
//
// Substrate-fact-introduction (P1 procedure) per
// `docs/briefs/r3-substrate-s5-coproduct-projection-carrier-worker.md`,
// Director γ-ratification at gunb-ai/gunbc#828 c#4394369848. Closure
// predicate: §1.8 gates #29-#30 (T-Anthropic-Wire). Unblocks Anthropic
// Messages #1702 re-dispatch + the three already-briefed coproduct
// paydowns (`r3-coproduct-{1,2,3}-*-worker.md`).
//
// **Layering**: compiler-internal projection substrate, NOT user-facing
// language vocabulary. Contrast `dsl/std/serialization.dag::CoproductWireContract`
// which lives in `dsl/std/` because users declare wire contracts.
// `CoproductProjection` is consumed by the projection-resolver during
// REST-response coproduct dispatch — the `from`-path resolver reads
// this carrier instead of a `response_variant_tag: String` shim.
//
// **Single-keyed-fact discipline (P2 boundary)**: per-variant payload +
// tag-value live as one keyed fact (`CoproductVariantProjection`), not
// two parallel maps. A variant cannot have a field projection without a
// wire-tag value or vice versa — illegal-state-by-construction.
//
// **Path-(a) shape decision** (Director ratified #4400354502 over (b)
// `FieldRef` introduction): `wire_tag_field: String`, with structural
// identity carried by the `Map<VariantId, CoproductVariantProjection>`
// key invariant + per-variant typed `WireTagValue`. Aligns with the
// `services.dag:28-36` precedent that explicitly rejects parallel
// field-handle wrappers ("`InputFieldRef` … would duplicate without
// strengthening the structural invariant"). Fail-closed boundary
// check at fixture load validates `wire_tag_field` names a real field
// on the coproduct's variant payloads.
//
// **DeclarationRef debt — unrefined-any-declaration handle** (codex
// BLOCKING-driven retitle from Director observation #1's original
// String-alias disposition; full rationale in the import-site comment
// below). The carrier imports the structural typed `DeclarationRef`
// from `v3.spec.v3_l1`; the type still admits any declaration at the
// boundary (refinement-typing has not landed). Debt-paydown row at
// `docs/debt/r3-debt-paydown-ledger-2026-05-02.md` shares the #1175
// refinement-typing-on-`DeclarationRef` dissolution trigger with
// `MethodRef` / `CallableRef`. Sibling `VariantId` Map-key handle
// dissolves under the same #1175 surface.

module v3.std.coproduct_projection

// `DeclarationRef` resolves to `src/v3/spec/v3_l1.dag:76`'s
// structural typed declaration-reference shape. Selected over the
// `dsl/std/serialization.dag:16` `DeclarationRef = String` alias to
// resolve a tri-way tension at PR-α: (i) Substrate Mgr at #2164 c#…
// flagged the `v3.spec.v3_l1` empty-record characterization vs. the
// disposition'd-String-alias framing as a BLOCKING; (ii) codex
// non-blocking + subsequent BLOCKING (sha 0e185083 / 49523238) noted
// the v3_l1 carrier "resolves to a typed declaration reference" (not
// String) AND that `dsl/std/serialization.dag` was missing from
// `bootstrap_authority.dag` so the alias import would silently mis-
// resolve at bootstrap-materialization time; (iii) adding
// serialization.dag to bootstrap-authority push test-thread stack
// past 2MB ceiling (lane2 symbolic-cost test stack overflow,
// reproduced locally vs. clean on main). The structural typed v3_l1
// `DeclarationRef` is already in `V3SpecAuthority` (no authority
// gap), is the canonical structural identity per its own doc-comment
// ("substrate carries the typed reference forward, no name-bridge
// lookup at consumption time"), and avoids both the silent-mis-
// resolution and stack-budget regressions. The debt-paydown row at
// `docs/debt/r3-debt-paydown-ledger-2026-05-02.md` is retitled
// accordingly per codex's non-blocking guidance: this is unrefined-
// any-declaration handle work — `DeclarationRef` admits any
// declaration at the type level until refinement-typing-on-
// `DeclarationRef` lands (the same #1175 substrate gap that retires
// `MethodRef` / `CallableRef` per `services.dag:86-100`).
import v3.spec.v3_l1 { DeclarationRef }

// 🟡 SCAFFOLD. String-aliased variant identity handle. Keys
// `CoproductProjection.variant_projections` and ranges over the wire-
// tag-value map. Today's substrate grammar can't express a refined
// `DeclarationRef<VariantDeclaration>`; keying by string is the
// minimum shape until refinement-typing lands.
// **Dissolution trigger** (single authority — shared with the
// `DeclarationRef` row at `docs/debt/r3-debt-paydown-ledger-2026-05-02.md:107`):
// the same #1175 substrate-level refinement-typing-on-`DeclarationRef`
// landing that retires `MethodRef` (`src/v3/std/methods.dag:31`) +
// `CallableRef` (`src/v3/std/services.dag:86-100`) promotes `VariantId`
// to a structural typed handle (e.g., `(coproduct: DeclarationRef,
// variant: VariantDeclaration)`) at the same time. No separate
// audit-row / string-bridge OR-trigger applies here; the carrier-level
// dissolution is single-keyed on #1175.
type VariantId = String

// 🟡 SCAFFOLD coproduct (single-arm record at PR-α scope). Typed leaf
// for per-variant wire-tag values. Anthropic + REST both string-
// serialize tags at the wire boundary; the typed-on-our-side /
// serialized-at-emit pattern keeps the substrate value distinct from
// its String wire form. Single `StringTag` arm at this slice covers
// the closure-predicate consumers (Anthropic #1702 + the three
// coproduct paydowns); additional arms (e.g., `IntTag`, `EnumTag`)
// land additively when a wire surface needs them. Brief constraint #2
// binding: `WireTagValue` MUST stay a typed leaf, NOT collapse to
// `String`.
//
// **Dissolution trigger** (P5 tracked-scaffold requirement, INVARIANTS.md):
// promotes to 🟢 TERMINAL when **(a)** §1.8 gates #29-#30 close (the
// closure-predicate consumers — Anthropic #1702 re-dispatch + the three
// already-briefed coproduct paydowns at `r3-coproduct-{1,2,3}-*-worker.md`
// — all land and consume `WireTagValue` against real wire surfaces), AND
// **(b)** at least one non-`StringTag` arm has been added in response to
// an observed wire surface (refuting the single-arm-coproduct anti-pattern
// per `feedback_construction_over_ratchets`) OR the sum is explicitly
// closed at single-arm with a Practice-4 receipt naming the substrate
// observation that all observed REST/LLM wire boundaries are string-
// shaped. **Re-escalate to Substrate Mgr** if a consumer surfaces a
// wire-tag shape that `StringTag` cannot express — that is the
// substrate-fact-introduction event that fires (b)'s alternate path.
type WireTagValue
  = StringTag { value: String }

// 🟡 SCAFFOLD coproduct. Per-variant payload field projection. `Empty`
// constructor encodes "variant has no payload fields" (e.g., Anthropic
// empty-payload variants per brief §"Single-keyed-fact discipline")
// without representing absence as a missing map entry — keeps
// illegal-state-by-construction. `Populated` is a placeholder arm whose
// internal field-shape detail (a typed `Map<String, FieldShape>` or
// equivalent payload-field projection) is deferred to the first paydown
// PR consumer per Mgr-disposed sliced-follow-up — `feedback_construction
// _over_ratchets`. Dissolution trigger: when the first paydown PR
// consumes `Populated`, the inner shape grows to a typed payload-field
// projection (`FieldShape` introduced at that point) and a TERMINAL
// receipt lands.
type FieldProjection
  = Empty
  | Populated

// 🟢 TERMINAL at PR-α scope. Single keyed fact (P2 boundary): a
// variant's payload projection and its wire-tag value live together.
// Splitting into parallel `Map<VariantId, FieldProjection>` +
// `Map<VariantId, WireTagValue>` would admit a variant with a tag but
// no field projection (or vice versa) as structurally representable
// — per Director's openai-pro REQUEST_CHANGES correction at PR #2079.
type CoproductVariantProjection {
  field_projection: FieldProjection
  wire_tag_value:   WireTagValue
}

// 🟢 TERMINAL at PR-α scope. Top-level projection carrier keyed by the
// coproduct declaration. `wire_tag_field: String` per path-(a) ratified
// shape (Director #4400354502): structural identity via the
// `variant_projections` map key invariant + per-variant typed
// `WireTagValue`; fail-closed fixture-load check validates that
// `wire_tag_field` names a real field on the coproduct's variant
// payloads (analogous to `services.dag` PR-β `ParamToken.name → Map<
// String, InputField>` key validation).
//
// `declaration: DeclarationRef` is the structural typed declaration-
// reference from `v3.spec.v3_l1` (selection rationale at the
// import-site comment above). The handle is unrefined at the type
// level today; debt-paydown row at
// `docs/debt/r3-debt-paydown-ledger-2026-05-02.md:107` tracks
// promotion under the shared #1175 refinement-typing-on-
// `DeclarationRef` dissolution trigger (paired with `MethodRef` /
// `CallableRef` per `src/v3/std/methods.dag:31` +
// `src/v3/std/services.dag:86-100`).
//
// Asymmetry with `InternallyTaggedObject.tag_field: String` at
// `dsl/std/serialization.dag:49` collapses under path (a) — both
// `String`, no debt row needed (brief §3 conditional debt does not fire).
type CoproductProjection {
  declaration:         DeclarationRef
  wire_tag_field:      String
  variant_projections: Map<VariantId, CoproductVariantProjection>
}

// **Gate 3 multi-consumer demo deferred to first paydown PR — surfaced
// to Substrate Mgr (#2154) as DSL parser limitation.**
//
// Mgr disposed gate 3 (i) trivial in-PR `data anthropic_chat_message_projection:
// CoproductProjection = { ... }` demo at #2154 c#4400893282. Authoring the
// demo failed at parse time on the `Map<VariantId, CoproductVariantProjection>`
// (or `Map<String, CoproductVariantProjection>`) literal — both inline-record
// values and ident-reference values produced
// `expected field label, got StringLit("UserMessage")` parse errors at the
// Map-literal `"key": value` position. Existing precedent for top-level Map
// literals lives in `src/v2/*` and `dsl/std/*` files only (`single_punct`,
// `kernel_type_set`, `container_type_arity`, `expr_child_roles`); none of
// these have Record-typed values, and no `Map<K, Record>` literal exists
// anywhere in `src/v3/std/`. The parser surface in v3.std appears to lack
// Record-valued Map literal support — surface to lane as separate
// substrate-tooling gap. Gate 3 reverts to (ii) defer-to-first-paydown:
// the first `r3-coproduct-{1,2,3}-*-worker.md` PR consumes
// `CoproductProjection` against its target coproduct, with the Map literal
// either authored once parser support lands or via an alternate carrier
// shape (e.g., `List<CoproductVariantProjection>` keyed by a `variant_id`
// field) negotiated at consumer-PR review time.
